dustry":"pharma","confidence":0.9,"rationale":"The bill directly affects medical device manufacturers who produce ultralightweight manual wheelchairs by creating new billing codes and payment structures for their products."},{"industry":"insurance","confidence":0.7,"rationale":"The bill changes Medicare payment and billing procedures for durable medical equipment, affecting how insurers process claims for these wheelchairs."},{"industry":"health-providers","confidence":0.5,"rationale":"Medical equipment suppliers who provide wheelchairs to Medicare beneficiaries will face new billing requirements and must potentially inform patients of cost differences."}],"plainSummary":"This bill requires Medicare to create separate billing codes for ultralightweight manual wheelchairs based on the materials used in their construction, with at least one code for wheelchairs made with titanium or carbon fiber and one for those without. Suppliers would continue to receive the standard Medicare payment, but could bill patients directly for any difference between that payment and the actual cost of the wheelchair. Medicare may require suppliers to inform patients about potential out-of-pocket costs before purchase.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People on Medicare. Anyone who pays a medical bill.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"B001260","score":0.06427617152344335},"overlapCount":9},"meaning":{"percentile":97.14105196651398,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[{"kind":"state-industry","text":"Insurance is also the top donor sector for 2 other members from FL. That points to the industry being big in the state, not to anything about this member."}],"unattributedShare":0.5264844478546931}},{"billId":"119-hr-7","bioguideId":"B001260","cycle":2026,"score":0.061260165720508956,"matches":[{"industry":"health-providers","donorAmount":94753,"donorShare":0.09785267932291188,"billConfidence":0.85,"contribution":0.032617559774303966}